WEBVTT

00:00:02.009 --> 00:00:04.178
The time is the future.
The place is outer space.

00:00:04.261 --> 00:00:06.430
Into the endless depths of space,
where even light becomes warped,

00:00:06.514 --> 00:00:09.225
a young woman rides aboard
her beloved ship Luros,

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:12.603
straddling the universe as
a diplomat, and a girl in love--

00:00:12.686 --> 00:00:17.775
Eris of Catia. However, people
call her "Captain Eris."

00:00:38.712 --> 00:00:40.464
Mitaiken na no

00:00:40.548 --> 00:00:46.262
Me no mae ni kotae wa iroiro aru kedo

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:53.477
Hitotsu no oozora wo nan toubun dekiru?

00:00:53.561 --> 00:00:55.354
Tanoshii kara subete wo kudasai

00:00:55.437 --> 00:00:57.106
atashi tteba dokusen shitai

00:00:57.189 --> 00:01:00.568
Honne ga koboreru yo Blue sky

00:01:00.651 --> 00:01:08.242
Mou! Namae wo kaite okou kienai you ni

00:01:08.325 --> 00:01:10.035
Shinken ni nattara?

00:01:10.119 --> 00:01:15.291
Sou you no yada nante iwasenai

00:01:15.374 --> 00:01:22.047
Jun'ai souchi (Set up now) ugokidase

00:01:22.131 --> 00:01:26.135
Aseri to yume no kassouro

00:01:26.218 --> 00:01:30.014
Shiitoberuto wa motto gyutto itashite

00:01:30.097 --> 00:01:36.895
Saishinsouchi (Back up now) ugokidasu

00:01:36.979 --> 00:01:40.941
Anata no kokoro dake wa

00:01:41.025 --> 00:01:44.653
orijinaru ga hoshikute

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:48.657
sakusen tatemashita yo

00:01:52.995 --> 00:01:56.832
"Cat Planet Cuties"

00:02:07.301 --> 00:02:13.182
She was a traveler from far away,
and a time long, long ago...

00:02:13.265 --> 00:02:14.975
So we should keep Sirius to port,

00:02:15.059 --> 00:02:17.269
and dock from the direction of Gemini?

00:02:17.353 --> 00:02:18.062
--Yes.

00:02:18.062 --> 00:02:19.855
--All right. Thanks.
--Yes.

00:02:20.689 --> 00:02:23.692
You heard her. We're detouring
around the dimensional fault.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:26.195
Alter course 1-7-5.

00:02:26.278 --> 00:02:29.573
Ready the hyperdrive.
Both engines to full speed. Warp 9!

00:02:29.657 --> 00:02:31.742
Altering course to 1-7-5.

00:02:31.825 --> 00:02:34.578
Both engines to full. Warp 9.

00:02:39.041 --> 00:02:42.836
We've entered hyperspace.
All hands, secure from entry alert,

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:45.047
and return to your normal duties.

00:02:59.895 --> 00:03:02.189
Um... Captain?

00:03:02.272 --> 00:03:04.608
Hey, Lawry. How goes the journey?

00:03:04.692 --> 00:03:08.987
Most comfortably. What is the name
of that tune that was just playing?

00:03:09.071 --> 00:03:10.614
It's an Earth song.

00:03:10.698 --> 00:03:12.032
Earth?

00:03:12.116 --> 00:03:14.410
Apparently, it was mixed
in with the recordings

00:03:14.493 --> 00:03:17.413
in a report from the Earth
survey team the other day.

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:20.666
If you wouldn't mind,
could you tell me more about it?

00:03:20.749 --> 00:03:24.753
Oh, sure. Come this way.
We'll listen to it together.

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.296
All right.

00:03:27.464 --> 00:03:28.090
"Catian Ambassy"

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:29.258
"Catian Ambassy"
First, the overall outlook.

00:03:29.258 --> 00:03:29.758
First, the overall outlook.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:34.054
A large tropical depression
forming over the Marshall Islands

00:03:34.138 --> 00:03:36.473
--is moving north around a high
pressure system in the Pacific,

00:03:36.473 --> 00:03:37.808
--This is a nice song, huh?
--Is moving north around a high pressure system in the Pacific,

00:03:37.891 --> 00:03:40.561
--It sure is. This was among the CDs that Ichika lent to us.
--and if it continues to develop,

00:03:40.561 --> 00:03:42.438
--It sure is. This was among the CDs that Ichika lent to us.
--It could become a typhoon.

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:43.731
It's a nice song.

00:03:43.814 --> 00:03:45.983
Mm-hmm. Would you play it again?

00:03:46.066 --> 00:03:47.234
Yes.

00:03:48.819 --> 00:03:50.446
Sure is a nice song.

00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:51.697
Yes.

00:03:52.448 --> 00:03:55.951
By the way, Chief, didn't you want
to talk to me about something?

00:03:56.034 --> 00:03:57.995
Oh, yeah, about that...

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.960
The very first Assistroid?

00:04:05.043 --> 00:04:09.256
Yes. The first model ever
made by Catia is coming to Earth.

00:04:09.339 --> 00:04:12.259
When did Assistroids
come to be used by you?

00:04:12.342 --> 00:04:15.137
It was nearly a thousand cycles ago now.

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:17.514
Or as we'd say
on Earth, a thousand years.

00:04:17.598 --> 00:04:21.435
That would make it your
grandmother or grandfather, huh?

00:04:23.145 --> 00:04:24.855
So why Earth?

00:04:24.938 --> 00:04:31.236
This Assistroid was built to work
on the first space survey ship.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:36.575
But that spaceship also
became our first space shipwreck.

00:04:36.658 --> 00:04:38.076
Oh, what happened to those aboard?

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:42.915
Well, more than 800 cycles passed
before the ship was recovered...

00:04:42.998 --> 00:04:43.999
Oh...

00:04:44.082 --> 00:04:48.295
The Assistroid from that ship
apparently wishes to come to Earth.

00:04:48.378 --> 00:04:50.214
You mean that it wants
to see the outcome

00:04:50.297 --> 00:04:52.466
of the mission that
it could not carry out?

00:04:52.549 --> 00:04:56.595
| see. So then, what kind of
treatment are we supposed to give it?

00:04:56.678 --> 00:05:00.516
About that... I've been told that
we don't need to do anything.

00:05:00.599 --> 00:05:04.561
Huh? We don't have to
go touring the sites of Earth?

00:05:04.645 --> 00:05:06.230
Correct. As for quarters,

00:05:06.313 --> 00:05:09.399
| was told that we only needed
to ready a room at the embassy.

00:05:09.483 --> 00:05:13.445
So then, we can't do anything
but be there to talk to it, huh?

00:05:13.529 --> 00:05:15.572
Still, I think that having
someone like you, Kio,

00:05:15.656 --> 00:05:17.574
who knows a lot about
Earth there to talk to,

00:05:17.658 --> 00:05:19.993
will make for great hospitality.

00:05:20.077 --> 00:05:22.329
Far more than I would.

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:34.174
Mm-hmm, okay. I'll take care of it.

00:05:34.258 --> 00:05:35.843
If you please.

00:05:42.516 --> 00:05:43.642
What?

00:05:43.725 --> 00:05:45.352
A request to visit home?

00:05:45.352 --> 00:05:45.519
"Ploase let me taye three days off"
A request to visit home?

00:05:45.519 --> 00:05:47.187
"Ploase let me taye three days off"

00:05:47.479 --> 00:05:48.939
Well, that's fine with me.

00:05:49.022 --> 00:05:52.776
But, my lady! You're
going to let the kitty leave us?!

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:55.988
Don't be so dramatic.
It's only for three days, right?

00:05:56.071 --> 00:05:58.448
| can't take that! Not for
three hours, not for three minutes,

00:05:58.532 --> 00:06:01.368
not for three seconds!
| can't be without the kitty!

00:06:01.451 --> 00:06:05.330
This Assistroid has been
given to us by Miss Eris.

00:06:05.414 --> 00:06:07.457
It does not belong to you!

00:06:07.541 --> 00:06:10.836
You know, it's unusual
for you to want some time off.

00:06:10.919 --> 00:06:12.296
Has something happened?

00:06:12.296 --> 00:06:12.713
"My grandmothor is visiting"
Has something happened?

00:06:12.713 --> 00:06:13.881
"My grandmothasr is visiting”

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:16.508
Your grandmother?

00:06:16.508 --> 00:06:16.800
"Sho is our ansestor"
Your grandmother?

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:18.385
"Sho is our ansestor"

00:06:19.219 --> 00:06:20.888
Your ancestor?

00:06:29.771 --> 00:06:31.773
What's the matter, Eris?

00:06:31.857 --> 00:06:33.025
Are you worried about something?

00:06:33.108 --> 00:06:36.987
Huh? Oh, no.
| was just listening to my music.

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:38.906
You've really taken
a liking to that, huh?

00:06:38.989 --> 00:06:40.324
What are you listening to?

00:06:40.407 --> 00:06:43.660
A song that was on the
CD that I got from Ichika.

00:06:43.744 --> 00:06:47.164
It's an insert song from an
old cartoon called "Captain Future".

00:06:47.247 --> 00:06:49.458
Not again.
You're not a child anymore.

00:06:49.541 --> 00:06:51.543
You should listen to
something more sophisticated.

00:06:51.627 --> 00:06:54.296
| won't have you making
fun of Captain Future!

00:06:54.379 --> 00:06:55.422
Ichika?

00:06:55.505 --> 00:07:00.052
Captain Future is a space opera
written by Edmund Hamilton,

00:07:00.135 --> 00:07:03.180
and is a sci-fi classic
celebrated the world over!

00:07:04.556 --> 00:07:07.559
Listen up. In the world
of Captain Future,

00:07:07.643 --> 00:07:11.229
there are Mercurians, Venusians,
Martians, Jovians, Saturnians,

00:07:11.313 --> 00:07:13.231
Uranians, and-- hey!

00:07:13.315 --> 00:07:16.151
I'm being nice enough to
explain this to you! Listen to me!

00:07:16.234 --> 00:07:19.863
There's no way I can listen
seriously to that load of nonsense.

00:07:21.239 --> 00:07:24.284
The kids these days.
They just don't recognize greatness, huh?

00:07:24.368 --> 00:07:27.079
Still, it has dreams and
adventure, and it's interesting.

00:07:27.162 --> 00:07:30.582
If you say so, Kio,
then maybe I'll watch it, too.

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:41.301
It's a nice song, huh?

00:07:41.385 --> 00:07:42.344
It sure is.

00:07:42.427 --> 00:07:44.179
| think so, too.

00:07:44.262 --> 00:07:47.724
Maybe I'll copy it over
to my own private system.

00:07:47.808 --> 00:07:50.018
It looks like you can
buy it on Earth's network.

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:51.645
Still, it's strange.

00:07:51.728 --> 00:07:54.690
Earthlings haven't gone
out into deep space, right?

00:07:54.773 --> 00:07:57.526
But then, to think that
they can express the feelings

00:07:57.609 --> 00:08:00.696
of space travelers so well.
It's a wonder, isn't it?

00:08:00.779 --> 00:08:05.117
| guess that even among
different species, the spirit is similar.

00:08:06.201 --> 00:08:09.204
Picking up a ship warping
out on the edge of the star system.

00:08:09.287 --> 00:08:10.831
It's one of our ferries.

00:08:10.914 --> 00:08:12.791
It looks like our guest is here.

00:08:12.874 --> 00:08:15.502
Open a channel, and let's greet her.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:24.845
It looks like we are well
prepared for our reception.

00:08:24.928 --> 00:08:27.723
All we have to do now
is wait for our guest to arrive.

00:08:27.806 --> 00:08:31.601
Say, Eris, are all
Assistroids built in this shape?

00:08:31.685 --> 00:08:35.272
No, previous models
were bigger than these.

00:08:35.355 --> 00:08:37.649
Their appearance was quite different, too.

00:08:37.733 --> 00:08:40.485
It was only recently that these little ones

00:08:40.569 --> 00:08:42.529
started looking like this.

00:08:56.585 --> 00:08:59.713
Pleased to meet you,
Miss Eris, Mr. Kio.

00:08:59.796 --> 00:09:02.049
My name is Lawry.

00:09:02.591 --> 00:09:03.592
<i>"Welcome"</i>

00:09:03.675 --> 00:09:07.471
"Mensooree to O)inawa"

00:09:13.018 --> 00:09:14.561
Of course, a tin man like you

00:09:14.644 --> 00:09:16.104
--doesn't understand delicate human feelings.

00:09:16.104 --> 00:09:17.898
--What are you watching, Matrey?
--doesn't understand delicate human feelings.

00:09:17.981 --> 00:09:20.317
What was that,
you reject of a rubber man?!

00:09:20.442 --> 00:09:22.611
--I can't take this anymore! How about I roll up that body
of yours --Rubbish. If you've got time to watch cartoons,

00:09:22.694 --> 00:09:24.071
--and toss you out into space?!
--then spend it reexamining our strategy, instead.

00:09:24.071 --> 00:09:27.032
--Knock it off, you two. This is no time for quarreling among ourselves.
--then spend it reexamining our strategy, instead.

00:09:29.451 --> 00:09:32.370
Is that my Yun-fat
and the others' ancestor?

00:09:32.454 --> 00:09:35.123
They're referring to her as
"grandmother," so it appears so.

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:38.293
She's more of an android
than an Assistroid, huh?

00:09:42.047 --> 00:09:43.381
Thank you.

00:09:43.465 --> 00:09:46.510
When we Assistroids
were in early development,

00:09:46.593 --> 00:09:49.137
there was a strong notion
that we had to be people-sized,

00:09:49.221 --> 00:09:51.932
or we wouldn't be able to help people.

00:09:52.015 --> 00:09:55.727
Long ago, we didn't have
mass adjustment systems,

00:09:55.811 --> 00:09:57.729
so in order to make us
the same size as people,

00:09:57.813 --> 00:10:00.148
biological parts were used.

00:10:00.232 --> 00:10:01.691
Oh, yeah?

00:10:01.775 --> 00:10:04.820
As the ages progressed,
with centralized control systems,

00:10:04.903 --> 00:10:06.905
language reasoning systems,

00:10:06.988 --> 00:10:10.492
and irradiative dissociation
control theory being perfected,

00:10:10.575 --> 00:10:13.328
the Assistroids who came
afterward were miniaturized,

00:10:13.411 --> 00:10:16.832
and they would become
like these little ones.

00:10:16.915 --> 00:10:20.001
But why did they
change to this design?

00:10:20.085 --> 00:10:21.545
Because if we look
too much like people,

00:10:21.628 --> 00:10:24.089
others become convinced
that we are people.

00:10:24.172 --> 00:10:30.178
That turns out to be unfortunate,
both for us, and for people.

00:10:30.262 --> 00:10:32.055
Something that looks like a person,

00:10:32.139 --> 00:10:33.765
and can do the same things as a person,

00:10:33.849 --> 00:10:36.434
can at times elicit hatred, or fear.

00:10:36.518 --> 00:10:39.646
Especially by the act of speaking.

00:10:41.982 --> 00:10:43.108
For example,

00:10:43.191 --> 00:10:47.571
if these snacks were to speak to you,
would you be able to eat them?

00:10:48.822 --> 00:10:51.575
The ability to communicate so easily

00:10:51.658 --> 00:10:54.244
creates the illusion that we are people.

00:10:54.327 --> 00:10:57.038
Even though we are nothing more than tools.

00:10:57.122 --> 00:11:01.293
You don't mean...
| don't think of them as being tools.

00:11:01.376 --> 00:11:04.838
Of course, I'm not saying
that all people are like that.

00:11:04.921 --> 00:11:08.550
However, when people are
forced into extreme situations,

00:11:08.633 --> 00:11:10.969
they sometimes try to
keep their mental equilibrium

00:11:11.052 --> 00:11:13.471
by convincing themselves of that.

00:11:16.183 --> 00:11:18.268
These little ones are lucky.

00:11:18.351 --> 00:11:21.438
They get to be treated as friends,

00:11:21.521 --> 00:11:24.191
and they are happy for it.

00:11:25.817 --> 00:11:27.444
I'm back.

00:11:28.695 --> 00:11:31.156
What happened? You sure took a while.

00:11:31.239 --> 00:11:35.243
I'm sorry. I went to pick out some
teatime snacks, and got carried away.

00:11:36.536 --> 00:11:38.163
Um...

00:11:38.246 --> 00:11:41.124
I'd like to step out
and walk around for a bit.

00:11:41.208 --> 00:11:44.461
If you wouldn't mind,
could I ask you to show me around?

00:11:46.254 --> 00:11:49.216
I'd like to see the night sky from Earth.

00:11:49.299 --> 00:11:51.509
Er... uh...

00:11:51.593 --> 00:11:54.512
S-Sure! That's fine, Lawry.

00:11:54.596 --> 00:11:56.640
Well then, if you would...

00:11:56.723 --> 00:11:58.725
The bones of the creatures on this asteroid

00:11:58.808 --> 00:12:02.145
have a silicic acid
compound instead of calcium.

00:12:02.229 --> 00:12:03.605
What does it mean, Captain?

00:12:03.688 --> 00:12:04.856
Calcium must be difficult to--

00:12:10.737 --> 00:12:14.741
Sorry to spring this on you.
Yes, we'll be waiting.

00:12:14.824 --> 00:12:17.160
Teacher said she'd come.

00:12:17.244 --> 00:12:19.454
What's the matter, Eris?

00:12:19.537 --> 00:12:21.164
I'm sorry.

00:12:21.248 --> 00:12:23.917
By any chance, do you dislike her?

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:27.587
No. This is the first time I've met her.

00:12:27.671 --> 00:12:29.089
Then, what is it?

00:12:29.172 --> 00:12:31.258
Well, um...

00:12:31.341 --> 00:12:33.301
You can tell me, if you like.

00:12:36.429 --> 00:12:38.139
Okay...

00:12:38.223 --> 00:12:43.520
Those of us from Catia have
two points of view about Assistroids--

00:12:43.603 --> 00:12:45.480
One is that we gave them this form,

00:12:45.563 --> 00:12:49.442
and the other is, "Oh no,
we gave them this form."

00:12:49.526 --> 00:12:51.903
Ordinarily, it should be fine for them

00:12:51.987 --> 00:12:54.864
to have the same form as us, as with Lawry,

00:12:54.948 --> 00:12:57.450
but it took something
away from the Assistroids' ability

00:12:57.534 --> 00:12:59.452
to function as tools.

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:05.583
But might not we have been
the ones who needed to change?

00:13:05.667 --> 00:13:07.794
How do you mean?

00:13:07.877 --> 00:13:11.715
Up until Assistroids
started looking like they do,

00:13:11.798 --> 00:13:16.803
our forebears did many awful
things to the Assistroids.

00:13:18.096 --> 00:13:21.224
It got so bad that there was
almost a state of war between us.

00:13:21.308 --> 00:13:24.728
Our morals toward them didn't
become elevated to where they are now

00:13:24.811 --> 00:13:27.355
until just 200 cycles ago.

00:13:27.439 --> 00:13:30.692
Oh. But Eris,
that has nothing to do with you--

00:13:30.775 --> 00:13:32.360
Yes it does.

00:13:36.156 --> 00:13:41.119
The reason I am here where
| am now is because of my forebears.

00:13:41.202 --> 00:13:42.912
We are linked to our history,

00:13:42.996 --> 00:13:47.667
SO we cannot escape
now what was done in the past.

00:13:47.751 --> 00:13:51.212
But our forebears have already
completed their apology,

00:13:51.296 --> 00:13:53.757
both as a race, and as masters,

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:58.011
and luckily, the Assistroids have accepted it.

00:13:58.094 --> 00:14:02.390
Which is why there is no
point in apologizing any further.

00:14:02.474 --> 00:14:04.392
And so...

00:14:04.476 --> 00:14:05.852
And so...?

00:14:08.772 --> 00:14:10.732
And so...

00:14:10.815 --> 00:14:15.904
| don't know what
| could possibly say to her.

00:14:21.618 --> 00:14:24.079
So this sort of thing
even happens to you, Eris.

00:14:24.162 --> 00:14:29.459
All right. I'll handle speaking with Lawry.
Eris, you take it easy.

00:14:29.542 --> 00:14:31.544
Kio...

00:14:33.046 --> 00:14:36.007
I'm sorry, but if you wouldn't mind...

00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:42.389
| keep some elemental calcium,
to regulate the spaceship's cyclotron.

00:14:42.472 --> 00:14:44.724
Kakazu, you're getting pretty
big for your britches

00:14:44.808 --> 00:14:47.018
to ask your teacher to
drive you around like this.

00:14:47.102 --> 00:14:50.480
Ah, aha... Teacher,
| thought you might enjoy

00:14:50.563 --> 00:14:52.982
having a robot from outer space.

00:14:54.442 --> 00:14:56.528
Robo-legs, okay!

00:14:56.611 --> 00:14:58.863
Robo-arms, great!

00:14:58.947 --> 00:15:01.408
Robo... kitty ears?

00:15:01.491 --> 00:15:03.701
So close... so very close...

00:15:03.785 --> 00:15:05.995
| see that Eris isn't coming with us.

00:15:06.079 --> 00:15:12.085
Y-Yes. Eris had something urgent
come up, so I stepped in, instead.

00:15:12.168 --> 00:15:13.962
It's all right.

00:15:14.045 --> 00:15:19.217
Please tell Eris for me
that I do not wish to trouble her,

00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:21.928
and that it is all in the past.

00:15:22.011 --> 00:15:25.849
But Eris says that she
still bears responsibility.

00:15:25.932 --> 00:15:27.976
What I wish is for you and these little ones

00:15:28.059 --> 00:15:31.187
to always be happy,
and to get along well.

00:15:31.271 --> 00:15:33.273
However, to be on terms
where one feels responsible,

00:15:33.356 --> 00:15:38.027
or is made to feel responsible
is not what I'd call true happiness.

00:15:52.417 --> 00:15:53.751
It's pretty.

00:15:54.878 --> 00:15:56.880
As long as you're here on Earth,

00:15:56.963 --> 00:16:00.300
| thought I might have you
see some of the pretty sights.

00:16:00.383 --> 00:16:02.886
I'm glad. A place like this may be fitting

00:16:02.969 --> 00:16:05.221
for granting my master's wish.

00:16:05.305 --> 00:16:07.557
Your master? You mean
the one who died in the accident?

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:10.768
Yes. He was very kind, and brave.

00:16:10.852 --> 00:16:14.731
He was the best master I ever had.
| take pride in him, even now.

00:16:16.024 --> 00:16:18.359
That's why I wanted to come to Earth.

00:16:19.611 --> 00:16:24.199
As it happens, it was this
planet that he was headed for.

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:27.952
At the time, the number of
places that potentially had people

00:16:28.036 --> 00:16:30.163
that were close enough
to reach in our spacecraft

00:16:30.246 --> 00:16:33.166
numbered 3000 to the fourth power.

00:16:33.249 --> 00:16:36.085
Amid those mind-bogglingly long odds,

00:16:36.169 --> 00:16:40.006
he chose a course to come to this world.

00:16:40.089 --> 00:16:42.008
Why was that?

00:16:42.091 --> 00:16:46.054
| believe it was by chance.
If it hadn't been for that accident,

00:16:46.137 --> 00:16:48.932
I'm sure he would have
been the first person from Catia

00:16:49.015 --> 00:16:51.059
to come to this planet.

00:16:53.353 --> 00:16:58.024
That's why I wanted to come to Earth,
and do what he wanted to do.

00:16:58.107 --> 00:17:00.068
What he wanted to do?

00:17:02.362 --> 00:17:05.532
After the warp failure, we were
trapped in an alternate dimension,

00:17:05.615 --> 00:17:11.120
and as we spent a long, long time
there, he kept repeating something.

00:17:11.204 --> 00:17:12.413
That if we ever landed on Earth,

00:17:12.497 --> 00:17:14.999
and there were people that
could be called human there,

00:17:15.083 --> 00:17:18.795
he would look up at the
night sky, and sing a song.

00:17:18.878 --> 00:17:21.422
And it wouldn't be a Catian song, either.

00:17:21.506 --> 00:17:25.176
He would sing a song
from that world. That's why.

00:17:28.888 --> 00:17:30.515
Um...

00:17:30.598 --> 00:17:31.558
Yes?

00:17:31.641 --> 00:17:35.186
Would it be okay if I heard it, too?

00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:37.272
Yes, of course.

00:17:38.523 --> 00:17:46.739
D I am a lonely spaceman )

00:17:46.823 --> 00:17:53.538
> All alone, a spaceman )

00:17:54.789 --> 00:18:03.506
D With no world to call my own )

00:18:03.590 --> 00:18:12.056
D nor home waiting for me )

00:18:15.268 --> 00:18:19.564
» Each and every world, )

00:18:19.647 --> 00:18:23.067
D each and every moon )

00:18:23.151 --> 00:18:33.953
D I've lived on every single one )

00:18:35.204 --> 00:18:43.254
> But what I like most of all >

00:18:43.338 --> 00:18:51.262
D is traveling alone from world to world )

00:18:52.555 --> 00:19:00.813
D I am a lonely spaceman )

00:19:00.897 --> 00:19:08.863
> All alone, a spaceman )

00:19:08.946 --> 00:19:17.580
» Will the dream I had across space J)

00:19:17.664 --> 00:19:26.631
D ever come true one day? )

00:19:29.509 --> 00:19:33.680
» Each and every world, )

00:19:33.763 --> 00:19:37.225
D each and every moon )

00:19:37.308 --> 00:19:47.694
D I've searched every single one )

00:19:49.362 --> 00:19:57.453
> All that is left is the wind J)

00:19:57.537 --> 00:20:04.836
D traveling alone from world to world )

00:20:06.504 --> 00:20:10.800
» Each and every world, )

00:20:10.883 --> 00:20:14.345
D each and every moon )

00:20:14.429 --> 00:20:24.397
D I've lived on every single one )

00:20:26.441 --> 00:20:34.490
> But what I like most of all >

00:20:34.574 --> 00:20:42.832
D is traveling alone from world to world )

00:20:52.049 --> 00:20:57.305
And so, the grand first
Assistroid, Lawry, left Earth.

00:21:03.603 --> 00:21:06.814
What? You left everything up to Kio?

00:21:06.898 --> 00:21:08.024
Yes...

00:21:08.107 --> 00:21:11.569
What a pity.
Lawry is a living witness to history.

00:21:11.652 --> 00:21:13.237
| feel so ashamed.

00:21:14.447 --> 00:21:16.449
It was a valuable experience for you, Kio.

00:21:16.532 --> 00:21:18.367
It will probably never happen again.

00:21:18.451 --> 00:21:20.995
Is Lawry returning to your home planet?

00:21:21.078 --> 00:21:24.624
No, her remaining operational time...

00:21:24.707 --> 00:21:27.335
her life will not last much longer.

00:21:29.003 --> 00:21:31.506
Assistroids who go more than two cycles

00:21:31.589 --> 00:21:34.550
without being recalled
after losing their masters

00:21:34.634 --> 00:21:36.385
are given the right to choose a new master,

00:21:36.469 --> 00:21:39.722
or to refuse measures
that will prolong their life.

00:21:40.807 --> 00:21:43.893
Lawry has invoked the latter.

00:21:43.976 --> 00:21:46.354
Then, her life will last...

00:21:46.437 --> 00:21:49.315
It could be as soon as half a cycle.

00:21:49.398 --> 00:21:51.859
The lifetime of her biological
parts is indefinite, you see.

00:21:51.943 --> 00:21:56.280
We can't make a clear estimate,
unlike Assistroids nowadays.

00:21:57.281 --> 00:22:00.201
Typhoon 17 is now over the Pacific,

00:22:00.284 --> 00:22:03.246
roughly 400 km south of
Ishigaki Island, moving northward...

00:22:09.710 --> 00:22:12.380
These little ones are lucky.

00:22:15.633 --> 00:22:17.218
"Mastor, something tho matter?"

00:22:17.885 --> 00:22:22.515
I'm fine. I was just thinking about something.

00:22:22.598 --> 00:22:24.517
Hey, yeah, Sadayan...

00:22:25.434 --> 00:22:28.020
Is there any way you can fix this guy?

00:22:28.020 --> 00:22:28.229
"You want ma to take a cracy at him?"
Is there any way you can fix this guy?

00:22:28.229 --> 00:22:29.981
"You want ma to take a cracy at him?"

00:22:30.356 --> 00:22:32.942
Mm-hmm, if you please.

00:22:33.025 --> 00:22:34.694
You do that,

00:22:34.777 --> 00:22:36.362
partner.

00:22:51.252 --> 00:22:53.337
I'm sorry to put you out,

00:22:53.421 --> 00:22:55.756
but I would very much
like to look at it until the end.

00:22:55.840 --> 00:23:00.887
| don't mind.
The planet is special to us, too.

00:23:00.970 --> 00:23:03.014
By the way, there's
a song I'd like to listen to

00:23:03.097 --> 00:23:04.891
while we admire the scenery.

00:23:04.974 --> 00:23:06.851
Would that be okay?

00:23:06.934 --> 00:23:10.646
Yes. I was just thinking
of asking you myself.

00:23:31.375 --> 00:23:39.675
I am a lonely spaceman

00:23:39.759 --> 00:23:47.725
All alone, a spaceman

00:23:47.808 --> 00:23:56.359
With no world to call my own

00:23:56.442 --> 00:24:08.204
nor home waiting for me

00:24:08.287 --> 00:24:16.045
Each and every world,
each and every moon

00:24:16.128 --> 00:24:28.057
I've lived on every single one

00:24:28.140 --> 00:24:36.190
But what I like most of all

00:24:36.273 --> 00:24:43.906
is traveling alone
from world to world

00:25:19.817 --> 00:25:21.569
Wrap your burning love with a ribbon,

00:25:21.652 --> 00:25:23.404
and choose a present for your boyfriend!

00:25:23.487 --> 00:25:25.197
Santa Claus [Santa Kurousu]
and Christmas [Kurisumasu]!

00:25:25.281 --> 00:25:27.533
Terrible hardship [Sanzan Kuroushi]
and suffering [Kurushimimasu]!

00:25:27.616 --> 00:25:30.077
Next time, "We Came After You."

00:25:30.161 --> 00:25:33.247
I'm coming to drop in on you!

00:25:37.501 --> 00:25:38.544
"See you next time!"
